      ":question/id": "f006d134-978e-5efb-b981-8cb6932a4901",
      ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 & -9 \\\\ -9 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{32}=0$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{32}=-4+(-1)\\cdot (-4)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S &=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 & -9 \\\\ -9 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 & -9 \\\\ -9 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 16 & 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{2}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
